w(F,"CRW Grant Application","Fundraising/CRW Grant Application",gd('12MgvrkDENL-ppLEcbuQvAO3ueuU6G8tj3xqxZCjoHvA'),'doc','2018-05-01','high',['grants','fundraising','learning-festivals','budget-finance'],"Completed grant application (dated 5/1/18) asking $4,000, with 9 LF locations and dates, workshop names, and the $25,000 cost breakdown. Good reusable template for any club/foundation grant.","""
**Date:** 5/1/18. **Org:** Spokes America. **Contact:** Kate Pearce, kpearce@mit.edu, 224-567-2524. Website mitspokes.com. Mailing address: Spokes America, MIT Edgerton Center, 77 Massachusetts Ave Rm 4-408, Cambridge, MA 02139. Nonprofit 501(c)(3); Tax-ID 04-2103594 (MIT). Not part of government.

**Budget context:** current funds $6,000; project cost $25,000; proposed grant $4,000.

**Program:** 8 students, 8 bikes, 3,500 miles, 75 days, DC to San Francisco, 9 schools/community centers:
Louisa County Library VA (June 1); Challenger Learning Center KY (June 13-14); Lab: Revolution MO (June 23); St. Louis Homeschool Connection MO (June 26); aSTEAM Village MO (July 2); Newton Public Library KS (July 5); Loveland Public Library CO (July 14); Christa McAuliffe Space Center UT (July 21); Carson City Public Library NV (July 31).

Four workshops at each stop: "3...2...1...Build!", "Circuits Galore!", "Playing with Python", "Picture This: The Science of Photography", adaptable for elementary to high school.

**Team pitch:** 6th year; guidance from past teams; an experienced cyclist from MIT Cycling Club; planned entire trip themselves while in contact with MIT staff.

**Cost breakdown ($25,000):** ~$10,000 bikes + gear + camping; $6,000 van rental and gas; $8,000 food and misc supplies; $1,000 teaching materials and emergencies. Raised so far: $5,000 ($3,000 MIT departments, $2,000 individual donors).

**Benefits / recognition / success measures:** project-based STEM in rural areas, breaking stereotypes of engineers, promoting cycling. Club recognized on website, Instagram, Facebook. Success = making it across and teaching at 9 schools, surveying schools afterwards, being invited back (which has happened for 5 years).
""")
w(F,"Grant Application Information","Fundraising/Grant Application Information",gd('1If6pfr-AKS7tAFw6Qj2sW6jnj53PGUGf0qRRA607v5o'),'doc','2018-04-30','high',['grants','fundraising','mit-admin','safety'],"Boilerplate bank for grant forms: MIT tax ID, Edgerton address, giving account number, mission, history, grant purpose, team overview and safety statement. Copy/paste source for 2027 applications.","""
- MIT Tax ID: 04-2103594
- Address: Spokes America, MIT Edgerton Center, 77 Massachusetts Ave Rm 4-408, Cambridge, MA 02139
- MIT giving page: https://giving.mit.edu/search/node/Spokes ; Account number 2530032

**Mission:** Spokes America brings MIT students cycling across the country, teaching students in middle America to engage with the scientific world through Learning Festivals at schools, libraries, museums and summer camps, while defying stereotypes about scientists (athletic, community-engaged).

**Organization overview (2018):** smallest but most dedicated team to date; students from MIT and Harvard; several on fundraising, a couple on school outreach, two on route and lodging, one on social media; mentorship from past teams.

**History:** 2018 is the sixth year; since 2013, 8-10 MIT and Harvard students per year to rural towns such as Hazard, Kentucky and Newton, Kansas. All past years completed the journey.

**Grant purpose:** inspire kids to ask questions, challenge the notion that STEM students are not athletic; funds buy educational supplies, food, bikes, camping equipment.

**Safety First (reusable text):** no Spokes team member has ever been injured on the road; keep a tight schedule to avoid arriving after dark; scout locations; purchase all safety gear (helmets, reflective vests, lighting); use the van for extra safety, stop if uncomfortable riding; previous teams compiled route difficulty/condition info.
""")
w(F,"Newest MIT Spokes Flyer","Fundraising/Newest MIT Spokes Flyer.pdf",gf('1t0KU_WjU3Wo66HfYmWLOxWgb3Rr-OIko'),'pdf','2018-04-21','medium',['fundraising','sponsorship','social-media'],"Final 2018 fundraising flyer text (8 students, 8 bikes, 3,500 miles, 75 days) with ask for in-kind and cash donations. The earlier 6-student version was discarded as outdated.","""
MIT SPOKES - 8 STUDENTS. 8 BIKES. 3,500 MILES. 75 DAYS.
8 MIT students biking across the country this summer to rethink STEM education. Website: mitspokes.wixsite.com/mitspokes.

**Who we are:** a team of 8 (freshmen, two juniors, a recent graduate) from MIT. Curricula complement each school's curriculum and highlight MIT's hands-on approach. Learning Festivals at schools, libraries and summer camps from D.C. to San Francisco.

**How you can help:** donations of any kind: teaching supplies, bike gear (or bikes), equipment and clothes, road snacks, water bottles, sunscreen, or money. In return sponsors are added to the Sponsors page on the MIT Spokes website.
""")
