w(T,"Department Email","Fundraising/Templates/Department Email",gd('1Po9SydmdCYg4w3eC5CI4xJmwzUg_1ZoB3abMQjUzJhQ'),'doc','2021-12-20','medium',['fundraising','communication','mit-admin'],"First-draft template email to MIT department heads asking for funding, with placeholders for the rider's workshop.","""
Dear [their], My name is [your name], a [year] at [MIT/Harvard]. This summer a team of 8 MIT students will bike across the country to teach STEM, through Spokes (spokesamerica.com; link to Boston Globe/BetaBoston article on Spokes 2015). As head of the [subject] department, would you help fund this program? I hope to cover [subject you are teaching]... STEM can seem intimidating or boring to youths not given enough opportunities; Spokes hopes they will believe in their own potential to do STEM. Best, [name], Spokes 2018.
""")
w(T,"NEW Department Email","Fundraising/Templates/NEW Department Email",gd('1JGgAVRbTsYeNAfXdZurPqRVE7NQwMoclzUAOW8unj70'),'doc','2018-04-16','high',['fundraising','communication','mit-admin'],"Improved department-funding email (by Bethany) that replaced the older template; personalizes with the rider's own workshop and offers updates/curriculum in return. Used to land MIT course money in 2018.","""
(Note from Bethany: did not like the old one so rewrote it.)

Hi [person], My name is [name], and I am a [year] in [department]. This summer I am going to be biking across the country with 7 other MIT students as part of Spokes. We start in D.C. and end in San Francisco, teaching self-designed STEM workshops at schools along the way. Many schools are rural, where elementary/middle school students may have had little STEM exposure. Details at mitspokes.wixsite.com/mitspokes; I will personally run [your workshop] where we will [details].

I am reaching out to ask if [department] can provide any help in funding Spokes this summer. It is an ambitious trip, typically costing about $25,000 in total, and anything [department] can give would be extremely helpful. In return we offer updates along the way, a more detailed curriculum (once written), and reflections after the summer. I have attached a flyer outlining the mission and needs.

All the best, [name], Spokes 2018
""")
w(T,"Local News Companies","Fundraising/Templates/Local News Companies",gd('1rk5rSDOYnrORURM3VjfZstgbiqcdgD60kuQ7LYJLCFE'),'doc','2018-05-02','medium',['press-media','communication','fundraising'],"Template pitch email to local newspapers in towns where the team would stay overnight, asking for coverage and crowdfund support.","""
Hello from Spokes! We are a team of 8 MIT science and engineering students. This summer: a 3,500-mile bike ride from D.C. to San Francisco over 75 days to host 9 Learning Festivals in small towns. Spokes (mitspokes.com) is a non-profit, student-run organization rethinking STEM education. Team: 5 freshmen, 2 juniors, a recent graduate.

Learning Festival: an intensive 8-hour day with 4 STEM-focused workshops (Computer Science, Chemistry, Robotics, Design) targeted at schools and libraries in the middle of the U.S.

We will stay a night in [town] on [date]; could the local paper feature Spokes? The trip costs about $25,000 (bikes, gear, food, van, curriculum supplies); small donations to our crowdfund (crowdfund.mit.edu/project/10264) are appreciated, but even getting the word out helps. Signed An Jimenez and the MIT Spokes team.

Lesson: the news-tip form blast (10 Boston and Austin outlets) is in Potential Sponsors; this town-by-town version was written late (trip less than a month away) - send earlier.
""")
w(T,"Statement of Purpose and Project Description","Fundraising/Templates/Statement of Purpose and Project Description",gd('1dKGX-KIOd5dohnvkmVM2bHpmj1qErzAHtAE2P6Grd10'),'doc','2018-04-30','medium',['grants','fundraising','budget-finance','learning-festivals'],"Short grant statement of purpose with 9-school list and a $23,000 budget breakdown (written by Kate, April 2018).","""
Applicant: Kate Pearce (kpearce@mit.edu, 224-567-2524). Project: MIT Spokes America 2018.

Statement: Spokes brings hands-on STEM workshops to rural areas; the cross-country ride shows engineers are athletic, adventurous and community-focused.

Description: 8 students, 8 bikes, 3,500 miles, 75 days; schools: Louisa County Library VA (June 1), Challenger Learning Center KY (June 13-14), Lab: Revolution MO (June 23), St. Louis Homeschool Connection MO (June 26), aSTEAM Village MO (July 2), Newton Public Library KS (July 5), Loveland Public Library CO (July 14), Christa McAuliffe Space Center UT (July 21), Carson City Public Library NV (July 31). Four workshops each: "3...2...1...Build!", "Circuits Galore!", "Playing with Python", "Picture This".

Team roles: several on fundraising, a couple on schools, two on route/lodging, one on social media; mentorship from past teams (6th year); since 2013, 8-10 students per year to places like Hazard KY and Newton KS.

**Budget total $23,000:** Teaching materials $1,000; van rental + gas $6,000; food $6,000; bikes, gear, camping gear $11,000.
""")
w(T,"Kate SWEcubator App","Fundraising/Templates/Kate SWEcubator App",gd('1LCWZrZd2068tvce-2pYntdD7HG2re-IZ3jNSkbDU2Wc'),'doc','2018-04-22','medium',['grants','fundraising'],"Answers to the MIT SWE SWEcubator funding application: requested $2,000 for gear and teaching materials. Shows what SWE asks for and how Spokes aligned with its mission.","""
Questions and Kate's answers (April 2018):
- Goal: bike DC to San Francisco, STEM workshops of own design at ~10 Learning Festivals; spread hands-on STEM and show engineers can be athletic and adventurous. Kate teaches a computer science workshop.
- When/where: May 27 to about Aug 8 across the country (VA, KY, KS, UT, MO, CO, NV and more).
- SWE alignment: exposing young girls to STEM, improving the image of engineers; team of 8 (6 women, 2 men) of varied majors, ethnicities, backgrounds; workshops include a mini lesson on STEM careers.
- Requested: $2,000, to cover gear purchase/rental and teaching materials (tents, bikes, power strips, tape, breadboards, etc.).
- Extra: each LF is a one-day, 7-hour event with four workshops; target ages 10-15 in rural communities; route planned day by day on a spreadsheet with mileages and elevations; need to reach the $25,000 goal.
(Application submitted 4/30 per tracker.)
""")
